WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.080
Oswald Cobblepot takes center stage in The
Penguin, but let's be honest — we want to

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.580
see more villains, more of the Arkham and
Wayne families' history, and high-caliber umbrellas.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.389
Perhaps one of Gotham's most iconic locations,
the Iceberg Lounge offers the criminals of

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:19.810
Gotham City a place to relax and rub elbows
with their crooked cohorts.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.270
While the lounge isn't expressly a villains-only
club, the atmosphere and clientele that the

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.820
business caters to is unmistakable.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.810
That's in large part thanks to its owner and
operator, Oswald Cobblepot.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.570
The Batman depicts the Iceberg Lounge as a
club in the heart of Gotham populated by the

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.720
city's most influential and corrupt politicians.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.640
In DC comics lore, the Iceberg Lounge is typically
utilized as a front for the Penguin's nefarious

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.020
criminal activities.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.621
Showing how the Penguin came to own and operate
such an establishment in the world of The

00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:52.329
Batman would help to further establish the
Penguin's character.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:57.170
And while it's not a story worth dedicating
an entire series to, a flashback in the narrative

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.840
to mark the occasion would be enough to do
the lounge justice.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.069
Criminals aren't born — they're made.

00:01:03.069 --> 00:01:08.020
That said, The Batman portrays Oz as the sleazy
weasel fans expect him to be, as he already

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.180
commands whole gangs of armed thugs.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.080
The Penguin might just show us how Oz established
the position he enjoys in The Batman.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.380
Of course, there's something else we all want
to know: Will the Penguin seize power following

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.689
Carmine Falcone's death and the destruction
brought upon Gotham City by the Riddler?

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:26.760
At the end of the film, we see the Penguin
gazing out at the city, contemplating his

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.470
future as a feared gangster.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.049
Clearly, now is the time to take control…
but will he succeed?

00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:34.712
"You better watch it.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:37.549
Do you know my reputation?"

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:38.806
"Yeah, I do.

00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:39.806
Do you?"

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.450
In DC comics lore, Oswald Cobblepot is subject
to a depressing backstory.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:48.560
In most iterations of the character, he is
violently bullied and mocked for his stature.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.840
Sometimes he was even given the name "Penguin"
by his abusers, and when he finally becomes

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.789
angry enough to furiously retaliate, he decides
to own the name, reclaiming it as a fearsome symbol.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:02.840
Other versions of his history tell a tale
of the unrelenting and harsh realities of

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.409
leading an impoverished life, claiming that
Oz's family lost everything after his father

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:11.460
died of a pneumonia-like illness brought on
by inclement weather.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.740
Oswald later takes up a life of crime to rise
out of the squalor in which he has lived for

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:16.740
so long.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.800
There are plenty of differing versions of
Oz's origin for The Penguin to choose from.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.490
One thing that is always true, though, is
that Gotham's criminals don't become gangsters

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.680
because they enjoyed cushy lives.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.709
Something steered the Penguin in this direction,
and it's a path worth retreading in the upcoming

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:34.345
series — it might even earn him a little
sympathy from viewers.

00:02:34.345 --> 00:02:38.210
The Penguin's most interesting relationship
in The Batman is the one that he enjoyed with

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.660
Carmine Falcone.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.659
Oz demonstrates his loyalty to Carmine when
he bitterly rejects the idea that he would

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:48.430
ever become a rat, even if it were toward
a rival, as he understands that Carmine Falcone

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.709
would have his head.

00:02:49.709 --> 00:02:52.390
Obviously, the irony of this later becomes
quite clear.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.319
Still, Oz and Falcone obviously had an unspoken
partnership, one that stretched back far before

00:02:57.319 --> 00:02:58.870
the events of The Batman.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.620
And while Carmine Falcone held the most power
in Gotham's criminal underbelly, the Penguin

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.019
wasn't far behind.

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:10.000
What led to his alliance with Carmine Falcone,
and why was he so loyal to the mafia head honcho?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.190
While Carmine might be dead in the present
day, dialogue or flashbacks might serve to

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.069
flesh out the fascinating relationship between
them.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:20.450
The Penguin of The Batman is a visually striking
foe.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.610
The prosthetics and make-up are so well-done,
in fact, that Oz looks like an entirely different

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.700
man than the clean-cut Irish actor we know
underneath.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.739
In-universe, it's clear that the Penguin has
seen better days.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:34.959
There is noticeable scarring all along his
face, indicating that Oz has earned his stripes

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:36.180
as a feared gangster.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.730
But what exactly happened?

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.750
How did the Penguin get those scars?

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.510
Could they be tied to his origin as a feared
mobster?

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:46.290
There's certainly an argument that, like the
Joker from Christopher Nolan's The Dark Knight,

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.450
keeping the scars' origins unknown adds to
the Penguin's mystique as a character hardened

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.749
by the streets.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:55.650
"You wanna know how I got these scars?"

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.730
However, the Penguin is a very different type
of character than the Joker, one who might

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.860
benefit from some further backstory.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.060
Hopefully, The Penguin reveals the truth behind
that rugged mug.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.500
The Batman begins shortly after the city's
major bust of Sal Maroni's drug operations.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.200
The headline news can be seen framed on the
wall of the mayor's abode, as the Riddler

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.640
quietly stalks him in the film's opening scene.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.380
Quickly, though, we learn that the drug bust
was a facade.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.810
When Batman follows the Penguin in an effort
to identify him as a potential rat, he learns

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.690
that production is alive and well.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.380
In other words, the drug bust was all a big
show by Gotham's most corrupt politicians,

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.050
and Sal Maroni was the fall guy for the display.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:38.160
Carmine Falcone, the Penguin, and their underlings
subsequently took over Maroni's operation.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.470
Clancy Brown is set to play Sal Maroni in
The Penguin, and it's likely the character

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.030
will have a few things to say about his relationship
with the late Carmine Falcone… as well as

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.680
the criminals who worked for him.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.780
The Falcone and Maroni families are often
portrayed as major players in Gotham City's

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:56.570
criminal underworld, having often waged war
against one another throughout the city's

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.560
turbulent comic book history.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.770
This could be good ground to cover in The
Penguin.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.300
In the third act of The Batman, the Riddler
partially succeeds in his goals, bringing

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.420
devastation to Gotham and nearly assassinating
the city's new mayor.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:14.180
Batman and Jim Gordon foil the assassination
attempt, but the city is torn apart by flooding

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.550
after the Riddler blows open the sea wall.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:21.100
Seeing the news cycle from his cell in Arkham,
the Riddler becomes visibly upset over Batman's

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.860
victory over his underlings.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.410
One shady character, however, offers the Riddler
a little bit of comfort.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:35.130
"One day you're on top, the next you're a
clown…"

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:39.260
At this stage, we all know that the neighboring
cell mate is none other than the Joker, played

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.810
by Barry Keoghan.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:45.220
Since the Joker is already in Arkham, fans
want to know: How exactly did he get there?

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.479
Has he already gone full-blown Joker?

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:52.260
Matt Reeves stated that the character is definitely
in the proto-Joker stage and isn't quite yet

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.070
the villain we all know and love.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.591
But something must have occurred to land him
in Arkham.

00:05:56.591 --> 00:06:00.789
Perhaps the Penguin series might offer a few
hints regarding Joker's previous encounters

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:01.789
with the Batman.

00:06:01.789 --> 00:06:02.789
Speaking of which…

00:06:03.059 --> 00:06:06.871
In the opening moments of the film, The Batman
offers a brief glimpse at how the criminals

00:06:06.871 --> 00:06:09.050
of Gotham see the Caped Crusader.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.520
As the Bat signal lights up the night sky,
an array of robbers and vandals are seen quaking

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.000
in their boots at the very sight of the dark.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.280
Michael Giacchino's swelling musical score
only emphasizes the dread criminals begin

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.220
to feel when they think Batman might be hot
on their heels.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.891
With The Penguin focused solely on the Penguin,
it's likely we won't see much of Batman, if

00:06:27.891 --> 00:06:28.970
anything at all.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:33.289
If we do, it may be no more than a few shadowy
glimpses of the character, or a handful of

00:06:33.289 --> 00:06:36.259
quick and flashy action sequences that don't
reveal much.

00:06:36.259 --> 00:06:40.370
Regardless, it would be a welcome change in
perspective to see the Penguin and his goons

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:46.380
face down the threat of the Batman, a larger-than-life
monster who seems to stalk every shadow in Gotham.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.220
In the comic books, the Penguin often has
his trusty trick umbrella at the ready.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.560
In most cases, the umbrella doubles as a firearm,
so he can surprise his targets should the

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.770
occasion arise.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.770
In The Batman, Oz is only briefly seen with
an umbrella at the mayor's funeral.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.570
This may have been just an ordinary umbrella,
but it could equally have concealed a deadly

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:07.120
weapon — although you probably shouldn't
expect much more than that.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.800
While the Penguin's umbrella can perform a
multitude of functions in the comics, the

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:15.050
more grounded reality in which Matt Reeves
has based his Batman world limits the uses

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:20.430
of a cartoonish trick umbrella — if it appears
at all, it's likely to hide a firearm at most.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.050
But that doesn't mean it wouldn't be fun to
see.

00:07:22.676 --> 00:07:27.350
The Batman did a great job of providing fans
with evidence that a much bigger Gotham lies

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.240
just outside the bounds of the main narrative.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.041
Many of these easter eggs hark back to the
comics: For example, we saw a reference to

00:07:34.041 --> 00:07:38.520
Edward Elliot, the man who, in comic book
lore, helped modernize Gotham City.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:42.870
In The Batman, he is the reporter who was
slain by Carmine Falcone as a "favor" for

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:43.870
Thomas Wayne.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.560
This suggests that we may be looking at a
potential Hush storyline for future sequels,

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:52.500
since, in the comics, Elliot's great-great-grandson
becomes the villain known by that name.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.716
The Penguin has an even better chance to highlight
famous DC comics characters in Batman's world, however.

00:07:57.716 --> 00:08:02.470
With D.A. Gil Colson out of the picture, it's entirely
possible that we could see Harvey Dent enter

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.150
the race for District Attorney.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:08.490
"Let's start this party with a bang!"

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:11.740
We might even get to see some more of Jim
Gordon's family.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.970
However you cut it, there are many opportunities
for The Penguin to highlight or tease characters

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.690
from Batman's long history.

00:08:17.998 --> 00:08:21.150
Gotham City is its own character in the world
of The Batman.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:25.720
The city is rich with lavish, creepy, and
seedy locales, many of which call back to

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.090
the Caped Crusader's comic book history.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.270
But The Penguin could take things further.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:34.090
Since the Joker has already made his entrance
into this version of Gotham, perhaps we'll

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:38.380
see Ace Chemicals, the famous chemical plant
where he became the Clown Prince of Crime.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.469
Meanwhile, if Matt Reeves and company one
day decide to bring the Boy Wonder into the

00:08:42.469 --> 00:08:46.089
mix, Haly's Circus would be a fine reference
for The Penguin to make.

00:08:46.089 --> 00:08:50.010
Meanwhile, Oz is sure to recruit some of the
city's most hardened criminals for his attempt

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:54.410
to take control of Gotham — perhaps a visit
to Blackgate Penitentiary is in order?

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:58.220
Clearly, there are plenty of opportunities
for The Penguin to broaden the scope of the

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.070
city that The Batman brought to life.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.779
In The Batman we learn a little bit about
Gotham's most prominent families, the Waynes

00:09:04.779 --> 00:09:05.779
and the Arkhams.

00:09:05.779 --> 00:09:10.610
Both families helped establish Gotham City,
while Arkham State Hospital is obviously named

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.089
after the latter family.

00:09:12.089 --> 00:09:16.070
Even more interesting, however, is that Martha
Wayne actually belonged to the Arkham family

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.940
before marrying Thomas Wayne.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:22.060
While Thomas Wayne targeted a reporter for
potentially unleashing damaging material on

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:26.130
Martha's mental condition to the public, it's
unknown if there was more that Thomas hoped

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.130
to protect.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:31.079
Of course, it's later revealed that Thomas
never had any intention for Carmine Falcone

00:09:31.079 --> 00:09:34.870
to kill the man, and felt intense guilt when
he found out what happened.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.910
He resolved to go report everything to the
authorities but was killed before he could

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:39.910
do so.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.360
It's a tantalizing story, and one that The
Penguin may expand further.

00:09:43.874 --> 00:09:48.649
There isn't a shadow of a doubt that, at some
point, the Penguin will seize power in Gotham's

00:09:48.649 --> 00:09:49.649
criminal underworld.

00:09:49.649 --> 00:09:53.680
Once he claims the late Carmine Falcone's
throne, however, what will he do next?

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:58.550
How does he plan to expand his empire in a
Gotham now emboldened by the heroism of Batman?

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:02.600
The Penguin is going to have to establish
his power through fear since his allies at

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.180
City Hall are likely no more.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:07.800
All of this, of course, means that Batman
will no doubt take notice of the Penguin.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.160
Does Oz intend to lead a campaign to bring
him down?

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.250
Either way, the Penguin is going to have to
deal with the Batman in the future, and it'll

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.369
be interesting to see if the HBO Max series
starts us down the road to that showdown.

